{"id":"hekeri","qid":"Q154226","category":"river","type":"hydronym","names":{"az":"Həkəri","ru":"Акера","en":"Hakari River"},"coordinates":[46.49764,39.69028],"coordinatesSource":"wd","region":"serqi-zengezur","regionSource":"wp-az-regions","admin":[{"qid":"Q301832","az":"Laçın rayonu","en":"Lachin District"},{"qid":"Q249252","az":"Zəngilan rayonu","en":"Zangilan District"},{"qid":"Q644048","az":"Qubadlı rayonu","en":"Gubadly District"}],"firstRecord":null,"period":null,"forms":[],"namedAfter":[],"etymology":[],"summary":{"az":{"text":"Həkəri (Əkərə) — Arazın sol qoludur. Laçın, Qubadlı və Zəngilan rayonları ərazisindən axır.","truncated":false,"source":"wp-az"},"ru":{"text":"Акера́ (Хакари, Хякяри, Акарачай,, Акерачай; азерб. Həkəri) — река в Азербайджане и Армении. Левый приток Аракса.","truncated":false,"source":"wp-ru"},"en":{"text":"The Hakari (Azerbaijani: Həkəri, Armenian: Հագարի, romanized: Hagari) is a left tributary of the Aras river in Karabakh, Azerbaijan.\nThe river is 128 kilometres (80 mi) long. It originates in Lesser Caucasus mountains and flows through the Lachin, Qubadli and Zangilan districts of Azerbaijan. In a small area, it serves as a border with Armenia. Its largest right tributary is the Vorotan (called Bazarchay in Azerbaijan), which joins the Hakari in its lowermost section.","truncated":true,"source":"wp-en"}},"images":[{"thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/H%C9%99k%C9%99ri_%28%C3%A7ay%2920211204_162208.jpg/960px-H%C9%99k%C9%99ri_%28%C3%A7ay%2920211204_162208.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","small":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/H%C9%99k%C9%99ri_%28%C3%A7ay%2920211204_162208.jpg/960px-H%C9%99k%C9%99ri_%28%C3%A7ay%2920211204_162208.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","width":800,"height":450,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:H%C9%99k%C9%99ri_(%C3%A7ay)20211204_162208.jpg","